# # /tamu/dc-types/
#
# Content-negotiated IRIs for the TAMU Digital Collections Types vocabulary
# (SKOS concepts for Archipelago Digital Object types and Browse/Search
# types used across Texas A&M University Libraries digital collections).
#
# https://w3id.org/tamu/dc-types/ and any concept beneath it (e.g.
# https://w3id.org/tamu/dc-types/ImageADO) redirect to
# https://tamulib-dc-labs.github.io/tamu-dc-ontology/, which serves Turtle
# or RDF/XML to a client that asks for it and a human-readable page to
# everyone else. All concepts live in the same vocabulary file, so every
# path under this namespace resolves to that same file (or to the matching
# #fragment on the HTML page).
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# Mark Baggett
# mark.baggett@tamu.edu
# GitHub username: markpbaggett

RewriteEngine on

# RDF/XML
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/rdf\+xml
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://tamulib-dc-labs.github.io/tamu-dc-ontology/tamu-dc-types.rdf [R=303,L]

# Turtle
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/turtle
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://tamulib-dc-labs.github.io/tamu-dc-ontology/tamu-dc-types.ttl [R=303,L]

# Anything else, including browsers and clients that send */*, gets the
# human-readable page. These rules have no condition, so the first one
# reached always matches -- which is exactly what a default is for.
RewriteRule ^$ https://tamulib-dc-labs.github.io/tamu-dc-ontology/ [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^(.+)$ https://tamulib-dc-labs.github.io/tamu-dc-ontology/#$1 [R=303,L]
